ust what was said in the  arguments today like I said it's very  close I could it Kennedy seem to be  leaning a little more towards the  government side but I think that that's  I'm not sure I would want to give odds  on that I don't go too far out on the  limb but he seemed to be more on the  government side and that would be five  votes right there and then Roberts could  make it 6-3 or could make could could  add another one to the to that side  making 63 but it could be 54 for the  government with Kennedy crafting this  federalist constitutional avoidance  argument and then the Liberals basically  just joining him in the outcome but  coming up with you know they would  decide with the administration now  there's another case thats related to  this the hall big case talk a little bit  about that and it does that the will  this case render that one moot one way  or the other it probably will render it  moot they're basically the same legal  question there they've come out of two  different Federal Circuit's this the  king is out of the Fourth Circuit  he'll bags under the DC Circuit how big  is on hold right now the administration  lost in the first round at the DC  Circuit but that Court is going to hear  it again with a full panel and that's  scheduled for a few months down the line  and I think if the administration wins  here then that's that settles that there  if the administration loses that settles  it because it's the same legal issue  when will the Supreme Court release its  verdict on ruling on this traditionally  case like this it's the last week of  june the court goes right up to the end  of june and then goes on summer recess  unlike many of us and so we can expect  at the end of june alright well we'll  leave it there thank you daman root for  talking to reason TV thank you we've  been talking with Damon rude about King  V Burwell the big Obamacare case that  was heard today oral arguments were  heard today in front of the Supreme  Court for reason